      "title": "Computing an Integral Using the Sum and Constant Factor Rules"
    },
    "question": {
      ":question/id": "7b93756a-23ab-5d6c-9fcd-27169e3285d1",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{2x^{8}-6}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\nAssume $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{2x^{8}-6}{x^{2}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(2 x^{6} - \\frac{6}{x^{2}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2\\int x^{6}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-6\\int x^{-2}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=2\\left(\\frac{x^{7}}{7}\\right)-6\\left(\\frac{x^{-1}}{-1}\\right)+C \\\\ &=\\frac{2x^{7}}{7}+\\frac{6}{x}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      ":question/answer-fields": [
        {
          ":answer-field/id": "a29dd043-d98c-5d30-aac0-965055ecdc63",
          ":answer-field/key": "selection",
          ":answer-field/type": ":answer-field.type/radio",
