      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/moderate",
      ":question/problem": "$\\displaystyle \\int \\frac{-3x^{9}-9}{x^{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x=$\n\nAssume $x\\ne 0$.",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Using the sum and constant factor rules, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{-3x^{9}-9}{x^{4}}\\,\\mathrm{d}x &= \\int \\left(- 3 x^{5} - \\frac{9}{x^{4}}\\right)\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-3\\int x^{5}\\,\\mathrm{d}x-9\\int x^{-4}\\,\\mathrm{d}x \\\\ &=-3\\left(\\frac{x^{6}}{6}\\right)-9\\left(\\frac{x^{-3}}{-3}\\right)+C \\\\ &=-\\frac{x^{6}}{2}+\\frac{3}{x^{3}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
